  "description": "Claude Opus 5.5 keeps each moved occurrence's ID at its landing and gives the occurrence left behind a new ID, sharing a lineage first written at the movement stage, as the prompt allows (\"either the landing or the occurrence left at the source keeps its id\"). Stage 3 raises V oku to I inside the new complex i-complex and relabels the lower copy t; stage 4 raises Ali to Spec-IP. Movement recognition required an untagged preceding occurrence to keep its ID at the source, so neither movement drew a path, the landing appeared at a construction step, and the relabelled trace replaced the verb before its moment. Both movements now play at their own moments with the source in its preceding form until then.",
