      "stageRecord": "The inflectional suffix -muş (the vowel-harmony variant of -mIş) is a finite I head. It carries the evidential or perfect past reading ('apparently read' or 'has read'); both readings use the same structure. Because the language is head-final, I takes the VP as its complement on its left and projects I-bar. I-bar then projects IP. The specifier of IP is not yet filled. One relation is established here: I selects the VP as its complement. This relation fixes the clause as finite, with the tense and aspect features of -mIş.",
