      "statement": "The subject Ali raises to the specifier of IP, where finite I assigns nominative Case and agrees with it, completing the S-structure.",
      "stageRecord": "Ali has no Case inside VP, and the specifier of IP must be filled. Ali therefore undergoes NP-movement from the specifier of VP to the specifier of IP, where it ends up sentence-initial. A coindexed trace is left in its theta position. Three relations are established, in this order. First, NP-movement forms a chain between the raised subject and its trace, so the Agent role assigned in VP is linked to the Case position. Second, the finite inflectional head assigns nominative Case to the NP in its specifier; nominative has a null exponent in Turkish. Third, Ali and the inflection agree in third person singular, and this agreement is also phonologically null on okumuş. The complex verb still realizes 'okumuş', and the final order is Ali kitabı okumuş.",
